# Machine identity -> profile. Read by install/machine.sh and hypr/machine.lua.
#
#   profile|sys_vendor|product_name|product_version|product_family
#
# Fields are the files of the same name in /sys/class/dmi/id, compared literally after trimming
# surrounding whitespace; a trailing * makes that field a prefix match, and an empty or omitted
# field matches anything. First match wins.
# A machine that matches nothing is "laptop" when it has a BAT* battery, else "generic".
desktop|Gigabyte Technology Co., Ltd.|B650 AORUS ELITE AX V2
# ThinkPad: product_name is Lenovo's machine type code, the model name is in product_version or
# product_family. Tighten with the real strings once they are read on the machine (machines/thinkpad/notes).
thinkpad|LENOVO||ThinkPad*
thinkpad|LENOVO|||ThinkPad*
# Framework: product_name is a guess until the machine arrives (machines/framework/ARRIVAL.md)
framework|Framework|Laptop*
